//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// HOW RADIUS WORKS
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*
radius defines LOOT SPREAD AREA

Example:

radius="100"

→ tight loot zone (military base)

radius="500"

→ large spread (farmland / countryside)

Bigger radius = more random distribution
*/



//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// HOW CHANCE WORKS
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*
chance = probability weight

Example:

chance="0.10" = rare
chance="0.50" = common
chance="0.90" = very common

IMPORTANT:
It is NOT guaranteed spawn chance.
It is weighted distribution.
*/



//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// HOW CLUSTERS INTERACT WITH TYPES.XML
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*
CLUSTERS DO NOT override types.xml.

Instead:

types.xml defines:
- item lifetime
- nominal count
- min/max spawn
- economy category

clusters define:
- WHERE those items appear more often
*/



//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// FULL SYSTEM FLOW
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*
1. mapgroupproto.xml
→ builds world structures

2. mapgrouppos.xml
→ places structures

3. mapclusters.xml
→ defines loot density zones

4. types.xml
→ defines item rules

5. Central Economy engine
→ combines everything into live world
*/



//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// ADVANCED DESIGN STRATEGY
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*

MILITARY ZONES:
- small radius
- high weapon chance
- concentrated loot

CITY ZONES:
- medium radius
- mixed loot types

FARMLAND:
- large radius
- survival loot only

COASTLINE:
- balanced loot spread
- beginner gear focus
*/



//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// COMMON MISTAKES
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*

1. WRONG COORDINATES
→ loot appears in wrong region

2. TOO HIGH CHANCE VALUES
→ loot spam everywhere

3. NO TYPES.XML SUPPORT
→ nothing actually spawns

4. OVERLAPPING CLUSTERS
→ unpredictable loot distribution

5. TOO SMALL RADIUS
→ loot feels empty or broken
*/



//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// WHY MAPCLUSTERS ARE IMPORTANT
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

/*
Without clusters:

- loot feels random
- no regional identity

With clusters:

- military feels military
- towns feel lived in
- survival progression works properly
*/



